{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'culture' %}{% set plan_short = 'Language, culture and learning' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Priority 6' %}
{% set plan_title = 'Language, culture and learning at the centre' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Make Anishinaabemowin, land-based knowledge and community teaching part of everyday family life, education, work and government.' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">The outcome</p><h2>More speakers, more teaching hours and more places where the language is used.</h2><p class="plan-lede">The plan supports fluent speakers, develops new teachers and creates a continuous learning path from early childhood through adulthood.</p></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>Speaker-led</h3><p>Fluent speakers set language priorities and teaching standards.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Family-centred</h3><p>Families receive practical tools to use language at home.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Land-connected</h3><p>Learning links words, stories, harvesting, place and responsibility.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Year One commitments</p><h2>Build the language and learning pathway.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Speaker and teacher baseline</h3><p>Record fluent speakers, teachers, learners, available hours and urgent succession needs with consent.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Paid speaker framework</h3><p>Set fair rates, supports and intellectual-property rules for teaching, recording and curriculum work.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Family language kits</h3><p>Deliver short, usable home lessons tied to daily life, seasons and community events.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Immersion pathway</h3><p>Design intensive learning for emerging speakers and future instructors.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Land-based calendar</h3><p>Coordinate camps and seasonal learning with Elders, harvesters, youth and schools.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Language in government</h3><p>Add language to signs, greetings, meetings, public information and staff learning.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Quarterly measures</p><h2>Count sustained learning.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Speakers</th><th>Learners</th><th>Programs</th><th>Everyday use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paid teaching hours and instructors supported</td><td>Enrolment, attendance, progression and retention</td><td>Programs delivered and cancelled</td><td>Departments and community spaces using language</td></tr><tr><td>Emerging teachers in development</td><td>Family participation and home-use feedback</td><td>Land-based days and participant hours</td><td>New public resources reviewed by speakers</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Decisions members make</h2><ul><li>Which language outcomes matter most over the next five years?</li><li>How should fluent speakers direct the program?</li><li>What knowledge should remain within the community?</li><li>Which public services should offer Anishinaabemowin first?</li></ul></section>
